From 3e7ad0be34ede5f71d82418ea203f7e1ce780536 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexey Lapin <a.lapin03@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:04:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: let the booth guide try the request again after the run
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

After See the new rule, the guide can take the visitor back to the case
the agent got wrong. They open a new chat, send the same request with
the same two Inbox files, watch the agent work on the new AGENTS.md and
open the letter, which now has no £0 bonus and no 0 shares rows.

The guide only offers these steps when that second chat can complete
without a model call the booth may not have. Once Versions shows, it
asks the new hone.guideRetry RPC, which answers yes when a turn cache
recording of the request replays from the project as the next chat will
find it, with the AGENTS.md that Hone's Pi extension syncs in when Pi
starts, or when
HONE_TURN_CACHE_RECORD=1 records the visit. Otherwise the guide goes to
the closing card as before, and the progress counts only the steps it
shows.
